-- title:
--   Blow-up chart surjects onto Drinfeld coordinate ring, kernel yB
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$.
--
--   **Level and field data.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is required by `hH₁` to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ (so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$). The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is required by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   **Base ring.** $A$ is a Henselian local discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field and with algebraically closed residue field $\kappa_A =$ `ResidueField A`; $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAq`), and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hζA`). $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$. The element $j \in K$ is nonzero and, by `hj`, has image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $t^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator series})$ of the $j$-function. Further, $\varpi$ is a generator of the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **The chart algebra and the supersingular point.** Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A K j` $= j$. The ideal $y \subseteq C$ is maximal (`hy`) and contains the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`). The hypothesis `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The two-chart model.** Let $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two maps from the middle chart to $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec} C$ and to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra at $j^{-1}$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. A point $z$ of $X$ is given, together with the element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ defined by `hϖz` as the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ through `toBase`, and `hz` requires $\varpi_z$ to lie in the maximal ideal of that stalk. A point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is given with `hy'` : its image under `ιFin` is $z$, with the same supersingularity requirement `hss'` for homomorphisms out of $C$ with kernel $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and `hy'y` : $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$.
--
--   **The formal local model at $z$.** $W_1$ is a complete discrete valuation domain, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), and $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and, by `hf₁`, $f_1 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, where $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ is [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18). Set $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v_1 - f_1u_1\big)$, with quotient map $\mathrm{mk}_S$. Then $e_1$ is a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ with respect to its maximal ideal onto $S$.
--
--   **The blow-up algebra.** $J$ is an ideal of $C$, and $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which, by `hB`, is the restriction of scalars of the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x\,\varpi_t = i\}$, i.e. $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$; `hCB` requires $C \le B$.
--
--   Write $\psi : C \to S$ for the composite of the germ map `germY` (the germ at $z$, over the open image of `ιFin`, of the section corresponding to an element of $C$), the map into the adic completion of the stalk, and $e_1$; write $\mathfrak{m}_S = \big(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi),\,\mathrm{mk}_S X_0,\,\mathrm{mk}_S X_1\big)$ and $\mathfrak{c}_S = \big(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\,\mathrm{mk}_S X_0,\,\mathrm{mk}_S X_1\big)$.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hbridge`** consists of nine clauses: the contraction of $\mathfrak{m}_S$ along $\psi$ is $y$; the image of $C$ is dense, in the sense that for every $n$ and every $s \in S$ there is $a \in C$ with $\psi(a) - s \in \mathfrak{m}_S^n$; $\psi$ carries the image of $a \in A$ to $\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1 a)$; every element of $C$ is congruent modulo $y$ to an element of $A$; every element of $W_1$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ to an element of $\sigma_1(A)$; the contraction of $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ along $\sigma_1$ is the maximal ideal of $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_S$ is maximal; every maximal ideal of $S$ equals $\mathfrak{m}_S$; and $S$ is flat as a $C$-module via $\psi$.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hcentre`** consists of four clauses: the ideal generated by $\psi(J)$ in $S$ is $\mathfrak{c}_S$; there is an ideal $I \subseteq C$ with $J = \psi^{-1}(\mathfrak{c}_S) \cap I$ and $I + y = C$; $J \le y$; and the image of $\varpi_t$ in $C$ lies in $J$.
--
--   Finally, an algebra structure `inst` of the field `GaloisField q 2` with $q^2$ elements on $\kappa_A$ is given.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $L_{\mathrm{loc}} =$ `Localization.Away (mkS (MvPowerSeries.C (σ₁ ϖt)))`, with $\iota_S : S \to L_{\mathrm{loc}}$ the localisation map, put $t = \mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$ and
--   $$x_0 = \iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S X_0)\cdot t^{-1}, \qquad x_1 = \iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S X_1)\cdot t^{-1},$$
--   using `IsLocalization.Away.invSelf`, and let $R_{\mathrm{loc}} \subseteq L_{\mathrm{loc}}$ be the subring generated by the image of $\iota_S$ together with $x_0, x_1$. Write $\mathcal{C} =$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), the quotient of $\kappa_A[X_0,X_1]$ by the principal ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q` $-\,1$, with $x$ and $y$ the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$.
--
--   Then for every ring homomorphism $\Phi : B \to L_{\mathrm{loc}}$, every proof that the image of $\iota_S$, the elements $x_0$, $x_1$ and the image of $\Phi$ lie in $R_{\mathrm{loc}}$, every ring homomorphism $t_W : W_1 \to \kappa_A$, every $c_R \in \kappa_A$ and every ring homomorphism $\rho_R : R_{\mathrm{loc}} \to \mathcal{C}$ subject to: $\Phi$ restricted to $C$ equals $\iota_S \circ \psi$; for $x \in B$ and $i \in J$ with $x\varpi_t = i$ in $K$ one has $\Phi(x)\cdot\iota_S(t) = \iota_S(\psi(i))$; $t_W \circ \sigma_1$ is the residue map of $A$ and $t_W$ vanishes on $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$; $c_R \ne 0$; $\rho_R(\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S F))$ is the image in $\mathcal{C}$ of $t_W(\mathrm{constantCoeff}\,F)$ for every $F \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$; $\rho_R(x_0) = c_R\,x$ and $\rho_R(x_1) = c_R\,y$; $\rho_R$ is surjective; and $\rho_R(r) = 0$ if and only if $r$ lies in the ideal of $R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ generated by $\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ — there exists a ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to \mathcal{C}$ such that
--
--   1. $\rho(b) = \rho_R(\Phi(b))$ for every $b \in B$;
--
--   2. $\rho$ is surjective;
--
--   3. for every $b \in B$, $\rho(b) = 0$ if and only if $b$ lies in the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $y$ under the inclusion $C \hookrightarrow B$;
--
--   4. for every $a \in A$, $\rho$ of the image of $a$ in $B$ is the image in $\mathcal{C}$ of the residue class $\mathrm{res}_A(a)$.
--
--   At a supersingular point $y$ of the integral model of the modular curve of level $H_1$ inside $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ — the level being cut out by congruence to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo the auxiliary prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ — this produces the reduction map from the blown-up chart algebra $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ onto the coordinate ring of the Drinfeld curve over the residue field of $A$, surjective, with kernel the ideal generated by $y$ and compatible with the residue map on constants. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_blowupChart_ringHom_localBlowupChart_surjective_ker_eq_span_of_dense_of_flat_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_blowupChart_ringHom_localBlowupChart_surjective_ker_eq_span_of_dense_of_flat_of_dvd), in the variant of the frame that also covers the small primes $q$.
